Description: |
  Approximate theory comparison to the neutron A1 column of publication
  Table I and HEPData Table 1. Uses eleven published x bins and Q2 windows
  of 2.5, 5 (nominal), and 10 percent around their measured mean Q2.
  Requires 1 < Q2 < 17 GeV2 and scattered-electron energy > 10 GeV,
  plus the analysis DIS guard W2 > 4 GeV2. The energy cut clips some
  x-Q2 windows. Spectrometer angular acceptances and efficiencies are
  not reconstructed. Uses free-neutron inputs with no additional helium
  polarization factor: the data already include the nuclear extraction.
  The MC estimator uses R1990 fit B and neglects eta*A2. E154 measured
  both longitudinal and transverse asymmetries, so this MC approximation
  must not be attributed to the published extraction. No g1 observable
  or evolution to fixed Q2=5 is performed. Nested windows share events.
